~ start
Intercom_Angel: [[Hi|Hello|Howdy]], testing the intercom system. Is everything working? Can you hear me?
- Yes
	Bad_Father: I can hear you, and I wish I couldn't.
- No
	Bad_Father: Nope. I definitely can't hear you at all.
	=> start
#- Start again => start
#- End the conversation => END
Intercom_Angel: No wonder you're going to hell.
=> END

~ demonstration
Nathan: [[Hi|Hello|Howdy]], I'm Nathan.
Coco: Hi, I'm Coco.
Nathan: What is your favourite food?
# "main" is referencing a DialogueStateContext node in main.tscn
$> main.favourite_food = main.ask_for_string()
Coco: My favourite food is {{main.favourite_food}}.
Nathan: Ok, if you can guess the number I'm thinking of you can have some {{main.favourite_food}}.
Coco: Ok.
$> main.correct_answer = roll_dice(10)
Nathan: Guess a number between 1 and 10, inclusive.
~ guessing
$> guess = main.ask_for_number()
if main.guess_is_number
	Coco: Is it {{main.guess}}?
else
	Coco: What did I have to do again?
	Nathan: Guess a number between 1 and 10, inclusive.
	=> guessing

if main.guess == main.correct_answer
	if main.tries == 1
		Nathan: Wow! You got it on your first try!
	else
		Nathan: You guessed it in {{main.tries}} tries.
elif main.guess > main.correct_answer
	Nathan: Nope. It's less than {{main.guess}}. Try again.
	=> guessing
else
	Nathan: Nope. It's higher than {{main.guess}}. Try again.
	=> guessing
Nathan: Well done! You can go enjoy some {{main.favourite_food}}.
Nathan: Do you want to play again?
- Sure thing!
	$> main.correct_answer = roll_dice(10)
	Nathan: Guess a number between 1 and 10, inclusive.
	$> main.tries = 0
	=> guessing
- Only if the number is {{main.correct_answer}} again
	Coco: Only if the number is {{main.correct_answer}} again.
	Nathan: That seems too easy but Ok. Guess a number between 1 and 10, inclusive.
	$> tries = 0
	=> guessing
- No thanks
	Coco: No thanks.
=> END